.TH CYAML_DICTIONARY_SET 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cyaml_dictionary_set \- insert or replace a key in a dictionary
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cyaml.h>

ccol_retval_t cyaml_dictionary_set(cyaml map, const char *key,
                                cyaml child);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Store child under key in the CYAML_DICTIONARY node map.  An internal copy
of key is made.  Ownership of child transfers unconditionally: on
success map owns it, and on any failure it is deep-freed by this
function, so it must never be freed by the caller regardless of the
return value.  If the key already exists, the new child is stored
first and the previous child is deep-freed afterward, so both may be
resident in memory at the same instant during the replacement.

child must not be map itself, nor a node that already contains map
somewhere in its own subtree.  This is not checked; creating such a
cycle makes a later cyaml_destroy(), cyaml_clone(), or
cyaml_serialize() call on the tree undefined behaviour.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
map    CYAML_DICTIONARY target node.
key    Null-terminated key string.
child  Value node (ownership transfers).
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success, ccol_invalid_args, ccol_not_enough_memory, or
ccol_container_full (the dictionary has reached its maximum
representable element count; not reachable in practice).
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_dictionary_get (3),
.BR cyaml_dictionary_size (3),
.BR cyaml_create_dictionary (3)
